    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d448">

                <pb facs="0386" n="374" xml:id="pg374"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.20/556a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wharton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-26T22:00:00-04:00">March 26, 1942—10
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>71. For McBride. The War Department in a letter dated March 17 has agreed to turn
                    over its road construction equipment to the Government of Liberia when no longer
                    required by the United States forces in Liberia.</p>
                <p>Further statement is made that the Liberian Government should be responsible for
                    organizing and equipping Liberian native troops, although War Department will
                    assist in their organization and training.</p>
                <p>With reference to the $800,000 to be made available under the million dollar
                    program, the War Department states that this amount will cover the cost of (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">a</hi>) constructing roads, and (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >b</hi>) organizing, equipping and supporting a native military force for
                    the purpose of assisting in the defense of Liberia.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
